WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:06.030
The Golden Empire of Yi Ti is the new Game
of Thrones prequel show that HBO is developing.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:11.850
It will be an animated show based on the Golden
Empire of Yi Ti, one of the oldest civilizations

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:17.340
in the known world which originated in the
wake of the Long Night and survived to this

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:22.990
very day. It’s at least 8,000 years old.
It was already ancient when the Valyrians

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:29.019
(including the Targaryens) were still shepherds
and had not yet trained dragons (over 5,000

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:34.840
years ago). Yi Ti is a great realm located
in the Further East of Essos and it’s the

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:40.429
supposed successor to the mythic Great Empire
of the Dawn, which, according to legend, fell

00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:45.899
during the Long Night. It’s ruled by a God-Emperor,
who is worshiped as divine.

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:51.569
Much as George RR Martin’s Westeros is inspired
by medieval Europe, George’s mystic Yi Ti

00:00:51.569 --> 00:00:57.920
is inspired by Imperial China. It’s a mysterious,
little-known part of Martin’s world that

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:04.269
will now be discovered to fans on HBO. House
of the Dragon, 10,000 Ships, Tales of Dunk

00:01:04.269 --> 00:01:09.030
and Egg and Robert's Rebellion are not the
only Game of Thrones prequels that HBO is

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:14.170
developing. HBO is also working on Game of
Thrones’ Prequel ‘Golden Empire of Yi

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:18.880
Ti. As most of you already know, The House
of the Dragon is Game of Thrones successor

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:25.130
show based on George R.R. Martin's Fire &amp; Blood,
a history of House Targaryen set 300 years

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:32.499
before the events in GoT. 10,000 Ships takes
place a thousand years before. Set 1,000 years

00:01:32.499 --> 00:01:37.079
before the events of Game of Thrones, the
series tells the story of a warrior queen

00:01:37.079 --> 00:01:43.170
Princess Nymeria and the surviving Rhoynars
who traveled from Essos to Dorne following

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:48.950
their defeat by Valyrian and their dragons.
Based on an ongoing series of fantasy novellas

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:54.050
by George R. R. Martin, set in the world of
A Song of Ice and Fire, Tales of Dunk and

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:59.420
Egg prequel series will follow the adventures
of the hedge knight, Ser Duncan the Tall (Dunk),

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:04.929
who would become a legendary Lord Commander
of the Kingsguard, and his squire Egg, who

00:02:04.929 --> 00:02:10.640
would become King Aegon V Targaryen of Westeros.
The stories begin with their meeting eighty-nine

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.659
years before the events of Game of Thrones
and will cover the events until the deaths

00:02:14.659 --> 00:02:20.390
of Dunk and Egg in the mysterious Tragedy
at Summerhall. This new prequel show based

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:25.750
on the legendary Golden Empire is the only
prequel that will not take place at Westeros,

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:30.930
but rather on Essos, to be more precise, in
the far east where the maps end.

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:34.959
Can we just pause the video for one second
and take this moment to like and subscribe

00:02:34.959 --> 00:02:37.640
to the channel
as this is the place you’ll hear the news

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:41.030
regarding all the Game of Thrones prequels
and let’s continue.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:46.230
Yi Ti is a region in the far east of the continent
of Essos. Officially known as the "Golden

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:51.370
Empire of Yi Ti", it lies near the eastern
limits of the known world and is sometimes

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:57.620
mentioned in the same breath as Asshai, indicating
its extreme distance from Westeros. Qarth

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:03.150
is located on the narrow straits at the western
end of the Jade Sea, and Yi Ti lies on that

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:08.870
sea's northeastern shores. People or things
from Yi Ti are referred to as "Yi Tish".

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:14.760
We have only seen one Yi Tish in Game of Thrones.
A Red Priestess that you’ve seen in Volantis

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:21.300
was of ethnic Yi Tish origin. In season 5,
at the Long Bridge in Volantis in Essos, she

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:26.170
preaches to the slaves gathered around her
that Daenerys Targaryen is a prophesied savior

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:32.030
sent by R'hllor. Tyrion Lannister and Varys
watch and listen from a distance; Tyrion mocks

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:38.251
her until she turns to face him, seemingly
knowing his words despite the distance. She

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:43.600
stares at him intently, forcing the two to
leave the scene in unease. This is the first

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:48.680
East Asian to appear as a character with speaking
lines in the Game of Thrones series. There

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:53.640
are people in the known world of the novels
who are ethnically East Asian in appearance,

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:58.590
and they live in the far east of Essos, far
east of Qarth and the Dothraki Sea, in the

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:04.650
great empire of Yi Ti (the narrative's analogue
to ancient China). As George R.R. Martin explained,

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:12.200
Yi Ti is so far away from Westeros that encountering
Yi Ti people in King's Landing is as unlikely

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:17.640
as encountering people from China in Medieval
England - medieval long-distance travel was

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:23.240
quite limited. In the novels, the only time
Yi Ti people ever appear is when Daenerys

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:29.690
Targaryen is even further east at the Dothraki
city Vaes Dothrak and mentions in passing

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:34.890
that few of the merchants at the city's market
are from Yi Ti. Yi Ti is one of the oldest

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:41.160
and most advanced societies in the known world.;
even the ruins of fallen cities in Yi Ti dwarf

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:47.230
the largest cities in Westeros. Many valuable
commodities - such as rare spices, gems, and

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:53.200
silks - are found in Yi Ti, making the region
incredibly wealthy; its princes are said to

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:59.601
live opulently in houses of solid gold, feasting
on meat powdered with pearls and jade. The

00:04:59.601 --> 00:05:04.760
capital of Yi Ti is in the ancient city of
Yin, with the god-emperor living in a palace

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:10.060
nearly the size of King's Landing, a heavily
guarded city-within-a-city. Unlike the other

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:16.000
ancient civilizations of Essos, such as the
Ghiscari Empire and the Valyrian Freehold,

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:21.940
Yi Ti never collapsed due to internal instability.
Nor has it ever been conquered by outside

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:29.210
forces. Thus Yi Ti culture has endured unbroken
longer than any other civilization. Yi Ti's

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:35.990
religion includes several gods but is focused
around two primary deities: the Maiden-Made-of-Light

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:41.720
and the Lion of Night. A few Westerosi have
ever traveled all the way to Yi Ti, although

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:46.900
a handful of adventurers have made the long
journey. Among them was the famous navigator

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:52.010
Lord Corlys Velaryon, known as the "Sea Snake"
who will be the main character in the House

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:57.290
of the Dragon. He sailed to Yi Ti and brought
back enough rare and valuable spices to make

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:02.740
the Velaryons, for a time, one of the richest
and therefore the most powerful families in

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:06.660
Westeros.
Yi Ti is known to be a real place, but most

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:12.160
people know very little about it, and it’s
still semi-legendary to people living in Westeros

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:18.080
(much more so than Qarth, but not nearly as
much as feared Asshai). Even the maesters

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:23.740
only know a basic outline of its history and
culture - in part because Yi Ti's scholars

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:29.720
greatly prize their delicate, millennia-old
historical scrolls, so they do not share them

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:36.400
with outsiders. Yi Ti has a long and extensive
history dating back 8,000 years. Since the

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:41.550
Long Night, Yi Ti has been ruled by eleven
dynasties of emperors: the longest lasted

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:47.630
seven centuries, the shortest only half a
century. Sometimes transitions between dynasties

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:52.770
were peaceful, other times they were violent.
Several civilizations have rival claims to

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:59.320
be the eldest, particularly Yi Ti, Qarth,
and the Ghiscari Empire. The Ghiscari Empire

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:04.800
originated before the Long Night and was still
young at the time of the cataclysm. Yi Ti

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:10.420
claims that it had an even older empire for
many thousands of years before that, during

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:15.520
the Dawn Age, but which was destroyed during
the Long Night and had to be rebuilt. The

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:20.860
tales of this Great Empire of the Dawn (as
it is known) are apparently mostly legend,

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:25.720
filled with emperors who lived for centuries
and warred with the gods. Still, only a few

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:31.140
generations separated the confirmed founding
of both; Old Ghis slightly before the Long

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:36.650
Night and Yi Ti slightly after - yet Old Ghis
was destroyed 5,000 years ago by the rising

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:42.420
Valyrian Freehold. In contrast, the Golden
Empire of Yi Ti is by far the oldest continuous

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:48.070
civilization in the world, both at present
and throughout recorded history, with culture

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:54.300
and accurately transmitted historical record
stretching back 8,000 years, to the end of

00:07:54.300 --> 00:08:00.690
the Long Night. In comparison, the Ghiscari
Empire lasted about 3,000 years and the Valyrian

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:07.180
Freehold about 5,000 years. The civilization
of Yi Ti is therefore extremely advanced because

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:11.841
while it has had its share of civil wars,
its society never truly collapsed in the way

00:08:11.841 --> 00:08:18.070
that western Essos did after the Doom of Valyria,
or experienced an effect as the Andal Invasion

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:24.060
had on Westeros. One Westerosi who traveled
there described Yi Ti as "the land of a thousand

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:31.190
gods and a hundred princes, ruled by one god-emperor."
The Empire lives in a constant state of war

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:37.899
against the Jogos Nhai, with many an imperial
general and three God-Emperors having led

00:08:37.899 --> 00:08:44.209
armies across the plains to bring the nomads
to heel, but such attempts seldom ended well

00:08:44.209 --> 00:08:49.720
and eventually, the Jogos Nhai raids began
anew. The Empire is also in danger from one

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:55.940
of their own Emperors who has been overthrown.
Far to the east of even more distant Asshai,

00:08:55.940 --> 00:09:02.120
the vaguest of rumors and black legends tell
of the strange city of Carcosa, ruled by its

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:07.009
"Emperor in Yellow" - allegedly the last of
the Yellow Emperors of Yi Ti, overthrown and

00:09:07.009 --> 00:09:13.879
exiled for practicing twisted dark arts. According
to the stories, the Yellow Emperor has managed

00:09:13.879 --> 00:09:20.329
to prolong his life for a thousand years through
arcane and unspeakable magic rituals, and

00:09:20.329 --> 00:09:25.970
he is biding his time in Carcosa until the
day when he will attempt to reclaim Yi Ti.

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:30.680
Others say that this is just a story told
in Yi Ti to frighten misbehaving children.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:35.060
We will have to wait and see. The Game of
Thrones prequels are coming. The House of

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:41.060
the Dragon is the first, coming in the first
half of 2022 on HBO. Many more prequels will

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:46.310
follow such as 10,000 Ships, Tales of Dunk
and Egg, Robert's Rebellion, and of course

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:49.920
Yi Ti which is currently in development.
Thank you so much for watching.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:54.860
If you enjoyed this video please give it a
big thumbs up and I hope to see you in the

00:09:54.860 --> 00:10:04.089
next one.
Peace!

